{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 8ce5 cream-capitate-snake — TDD held-out loop, phases 4a-4d.\n\n4a SPEC + SURFACE-PARITY CENSUS (5 slots): CLI verb = OUT OF SCOPE (this is a lint gate, not a\nCLI verb; none of the 23 sibling check_*.py are verbs). MCP tool = OUT OF SCOPE (no sibling gate is\nexposed as a tool). Library facade = OUT OF SCOPE (check scripts are loaded by path in tests, not\nimportable API, per repo convention). Automated callers = IN SCOPE, proven by a test asserting the\nmake lint wiring. Dual-direction = IN SCOPE: --check (read) and --update (write) both proven.\n\nGROUNDING PROBE (live, verified): 65 tools = 35 read + 7 llm + 23 write. Correspondence to\nrebar.__all__: 35 exact-name, 14 co_names-only, 16 with NO library counterpart (audit_trail,\nexplain_criterion, gate_status, get_workflow_result/status, plan_review_status, render_workflow,\nverify_completion_status, review_code, review_plan, review_plan_start, scan_spec, sign_review,\nverify_completion, verify_completion_start, run_workflow) — these are legitimately MCP-only and\nneed an explicit mcp_only declaration.\nKEY DESIGN INSIGHT: all 35 exact-match tools omit the library's repo_root (MCP resolves the root\nfrom the server env). That is a CATEGORY-LEVEL normalization rule, not drift — a naive param diff\nflags all 35 and the gate becomes useless. This is what 'NORMALIZED parity manifest' in AC1 means.\n\n4b RED-FIRST: authored 23 tests across a happy-path file and a held-out file, plus a no-behavior\nskeleton so RED fails on ASSERTIONS not import errors. Result: 17 FAILED / 6 passed.\nAll 17 failures for the RIGHT reason: 'assert 0 != 0' (drift not detected) x8, KeyError 'tools'\n(no enumeration), non-canonical JSON, no confirmation line, FileNotFoundError (manifest absent) x2,\nmake-lint not wired, '--update' absent from failure output.\nHONEST CAVEAT: the 6 passing are all POSITIVE assertions (parity -> exit 0, repo_root normalizes\naway, --update idempotent, CLI exit 0) which a permissive stub cannot fail. They are regression\nguards against an over-eager gate; their teeth come from the 4e mutation step, not from RED.\n\n4c HELD OUT: tests/unit/test_mcp_library_parity_heldout.py physically MOVED out of the worktree to\nthe job tmp dir. Implementer sees only the happy path (5 tests). Held-out cases: added/removed tool,\nmcp-param drift, changed library_symbol mapping, undeclared divergence, declared-with-reason passes,\nblank/missing reason fails (3 params), declared-divergence-shape-moved still fails (AC3 sharp edge),\nmcp_only must be declared, repo_root normalization, committed-manifest covers every live tool,\nedit_ticket divergence declared, --update idempotent, CLI exit code, make lint wiring, actionable\nfailure output.\n\n4d DISPATCHED implementer subagent with: ticket + ACs, happy-path oracle, the verified enumeration\nrecipe, the repo_root normalization insight, the 16 mcp-only names, check_verify_gate_parity.py as\nthe shape precedent, and the BINDING STRUCTURAL CONSTRAINTS the behavioral oracle cannot see\n(800-LOC cap / 200-500 target, complexity 15, ruff check+format, Makefile @# house style, fail-loud\non missing mcp import). Told it not to weaken tests and that unseen tests exist.\n\nCROSS-LEAF NOTE: my E2E test spawns the script with cwd=REPO_ROOT in a clean subprocess (same\nrationale as tests/unit/test_api_surface_gate.py:64 — escaping the unit tier's autouse\nmonkeypatches). That is exactly one of the 23 cwd=REPO_ROOT sites sibling washedup-ropeable-hammerkop\nwill flag, so it will need that leaf's opt-out marker with a reason. Recorded for the residual sweep."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788315546597180001,"uuid":"f9cbfdc8-aaff-488e-aeef-a2edf44386c4"}